[38;5;252m[1m## Behavioral equivalence[0m[0m
[0m[0m
I built a [38;5;10mdlopen[0m harness that loads both shared objects and compares the raw 32-bit patterns of the returned floats. Over every input where the C code's table indexing is in bounds — x from -16 to 8223, covering both branches ([38;5;10mx < 129[0m, the [38;5;10mx < 1024[0m shift path, and the [38;5;10mx >= 1024[0m path) — [1m8240/8240 inputs are bit-identical, zero mismatches.[22m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Details I had to preserve rather than "clean up":[0m[0m
- [38;5;10m2 * x & 64[0m parses as [38;5;10m(2*x) & 64[0m, not [38;5;10m2 * (x & 64)[0m.[0m[0m
- The cast in [38;5;10m(float)((x & 63) - sign) / ((x & ~63) + sign)[0m applies only to the numerator, so this is a single-precision divide with an int denominator promoted to float — and it divides by zero for some inputs, producing inf/NaN, which I left intact.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10m4.f / 3[0m and [38;5;10m2.f / 9[0m are float-typed constant expressions in C, so I wrote them as [38;5;10mf32[0m const-folds rather than typing out decimal approximations.[0m[0m
- Overflow-prone integer ops use [38;5;10mwrapping_*[0m so release-mode Rust doesn't panic where C silently wraps.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
One caveat worth flagging, since it's a real limit rather than an oversight: the C function reads outside [38;5;10mg_pow43[145][0m for x ≥ 8224 (its computed index reaches 145) and for x < -16 (negative index). I reproduce these as raw pointer reads so Rust doesn't panic where C doesn't, but the [3mvalues[23m cannot match — in the C build those reads land in the compiler's own float literal pool (256.0, 16.0, 2/9, 4/3, 1.0, visible in [38;5;10m.rodata[0m right after the table), which is an artifact of this particular compiler and optimization level, not library behavior. Mismatches begin at exactly x=8224, the first out-of-bounds index, and nowhere earlier. This is undefined behavior in the original, so there's no defined output to be byte-identical to; chasing it by padding the Rust table would be brittle and could diverge differently under any other compiler.[0m[0m
